borhood noted in the 1970s and '80s for drugs, blight, and a burgeoning art scene. His creativity spilled out in paintings, photographs, films, texts, installations, and in his life and its recounting-creating a sort of mythos around himself. His circle of East Village artists moved into the national spotlight just as the AIDS plague began its devastating advance, and as right-wing culture warriors reared their heads. As Wojnarowicz's reputation as an artist grew, so did his reputation as an agitator-because he dealt so openly with his homosexuality, so angrily with his circumstances as a Person With AIDS, and so fiercely with his would-be censors. Fire in the Belly is the untold story of a polarizing figure at a pivotal moment in American culture-and one of the most highly acclaimed biographies of the year.","publicationYear":2012,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-fire-in-the-belly-the-life-and-times-of-david-wojnarowicz-cynthia-carr"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Artists","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-fire-in-the-belly-the-life-and-times-of-david-wojnarowicz-cynthia-carr"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Gay activists","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-fire-in-the-belly-the-life-and-times-of-david-wojnarowicz-cynthia-carr"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Gay artists","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-fire-in-the-belly-the-life-and-times-of-david-wojnarowicz-cynthia-carr"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Artists, united states","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-fire-in-the-belly-the-life-and-times-of-david-wojnarowicz-cynthia-carr"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Artists, biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-fire-in-the-belly-the-life-and-times-of-da